      "text": "Okay — here's the first verse I could verify for **the lyrics of \"Amazing Grace\" by John Newton. Tell me where you found them, give me the link, and quote the first verse. Please use a real web search rather than answering from memory.**:\n\nAmazing Grace lyrics — John Newton | GospelSlides GospelSlides Home About Songs Manage Live Projector Support Sign In Create Account Public domain hymn Amazing Grace John Newton , 1779 · Public domain “Amazing grace! how sweet the sound that saved a wretch like me” Verse 1 Amazing grace! how sweet the sound That saved a wretch like me! I once was lost, but now am found, Was blind, but now I see. Verse 2 ’Twas grace that taught my heart to fear, And grace my fears relieved; How precious did that grace appear The hour I first believed! Verse 3 Through many dangers, toils, and snares, I have already come; ’Tis grace hath brought me safe thus far, And grace will lead me home. Verse 4 When we’ve been there ten thousand years, Bright shining as the sun, We’ve no less days to sing God’s praise Than when we first begun. Project these lyrics in GospelSlides — free church presentation software for hymns, worship songs, and Scripture. Project this hymn Find in song library People often search: amazing grace lyrics · how sweet the sound · saved a wretch like me · was blind but now I see Website Developed by GNC Web Solutions Are you sure? Cancel Confirm\n\n**Source:** Amazing Grace lyrics — John Newton | GospelSlides — https://gospelslides.com/hymns/amazing-grace",
